<%#
  The square mark beside the library's name in the bar.

  A school that uploads its own icon gets it here as well as in the browser
  tab: the mark is the same badge in both places, and having the tab show the
  school crest while the page kept a stock book would read as a mistake.

  The alt is empty on purpose. The library's name sits immediately beside it
  in the same link, so a screen reader announcing the image too would say the
  name twice.

  Expects: brandIcon.
-%>
<span class="bar__mark bar__mark--image">
  <% if (brandIcon) { %>
    <img src="/brand/<%= brandIcon.replace(/\.png$/, '') %>-32.png" alt="" width="24" height="24">
  <% } else { %>
    <img src="/assets/default-icon-32.png" alt="" width="24" height="24">
  <% } %>
</span>
